<title>HONG KONG: Wharf shrs plummet on court judgement.</title>
<headline>Wharf shrs plummet on court judgement.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wharf (Holdings) Ltd shares fell sharply on Thursday after the company said it would contest a US$125.5 million judgement against it in a U.S. court.</p>
<p>Wharf was down HK$0.70, or 2.4 percent, in morning trade at HK$28.60 in a rising market, after hitting a low of HK$28.35.</p>
<p>&quot;I wouldn't be surprised if a lot of people actually downgrade it to a sell,&quot; Clementine Ng of Amsteel Securities told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Sentiment is definitely against the stock. It's the second litigation that's gone against them in three months,&quot; said an analyst at a U.S. investment bank who declined to be named.</p>
</text>
